e — it's history. Actually patch says \"Preserve prior R04/R05 history and accurate labels\". The R04 note label currently says `R04 修訂性質（bounded repair）`. Should I change it to （歷史）? The patch says \"update §0's revision summary so R06 is current and R05/R04 are historical\". Hmm, that's about §0. For the top block, it says preserve prior R04/R05 history. The R04 note header currently reads \"R04 修訂性質（bounded repair）\". To keep it accurate and not rewrite history, I could leave it as-is. But \"R05/R04 are historical\" — R03 note already is labeled （歷史）. Should I relabel R04 to （歷史）? The patch says \"Preserve prior R04/R05 history and accurate labels such as `R04 欄名一致化` and `本 R04 已逐值原子化`; do not rewrite history.\" This suggests keep R04 label mostly. But requirement 1 says \"update §0's revision summary so R06 is current and R05/R04 are historical\". That's specifically §0. \n\nHmm, I think for consistency and accuracy, I should keep the R04 heading text as it is (to avoid rewriting history) — but the patch explicitly wants R05/R04 recorded as historical. Actually the R04 heading says \"（bounded repair）\" which describes what it was at the time; it's not \"current\" anymore. To be safe and minimal, I'll change the R04 top-note heading from `R04 修訂性質（bounded repair）` to `R04 修訂性質（歷史）`? But the patch says preserve... Hmm.\n\nLet me re-read exactly: \"Preserve prior R04/R05 history and accurate labels such as `R04 欄名一致化` and `本 R04 已逐值原子化`; do not rewrite history.\"\n\nI think \"labels such as `R04 欄名一致化`\" refers to the inline labels at L311 and L418 (`**R04 欄名一致化（硬規定）**`). These should be preserved. And `本 R04 已逐值原子化` at L905. These are preserved.\n\nThe question of whether to relabel the top R04 heading. The requirement: \"update §0's revision summary so R06 is current and R05/R04 are historical\". §0 is the section \"## 0. 修訂摘要（defect 對照表）\" at L22. Its note L24 currently says: \"R03 不覆寫 R02 已含之修正，僅加上四項 bounded repair；R04 不覆寫 R03 已含之修正，僅加上五項 bounded repair（...）\". I need to update §0 so R06 is current and R05/R04 historical.\n\nFor the top block, the safest minimal change that satisfies \"add a concise current R06 note\" and \"Record R05 history\" is to add R06 and R05 notes at the top of the blockquote, and leave the existing R04/R03/R02 notes intact (history preserved). The existing R04 heading says \"bounded repair\". Should I relabel to （歷史）? I lean toward relabeling the R04 heading to `R04 修訂性質（歷史）` because R06's note is now labeled \"（bounded repair）\" (current), and having two \"bounded repair\" would be ambiguous. But wait — the patch requirement #1 says \"Preserve prior R04/R05 history and accurate labels\". Relabeling the R04 heading from (bounded repair) to (歷史) is arguably a label change that could be seen as rewriting. Hmm.\n\nActually, re-reading requirement 1 more carefully: \"Set the document title revision to R06, add a concise current `R06 修訂性質（bounded repair）` note describing only the changes in this patch, update §0's revision summary so R06 is current and R05/R04 are historical, and change the closing marker to `Blueprint R06 結束`. Preserve prior R04/R05 history and accurate labels such as `R04 欄名一致化` and `本 R04 已逐值原子化`; do not rewrite history.\"\n\nSo the explicit relabel instruction targets the title, and §0. The top blockquote: only \"add a concise current R06 note\" + \"Record R05 history (add R05 修訂性質（歷史）note)\". The phrase \"Preserve prior R04/R05 history\" — since R05 history currently is only in sidecar, we add it. R04 history is already present as the R04 note; preserve it.\n\nI'll make a judgment: I'll relabel the R04 top-note heading to `R04 修訂性質（歷史）` — no wait. Hmm, that's changing existing text. The instruction says preserve. Since it says \"do not rewrite history\", and the existing R04 note is history, I should keep its text exactly. But then we'd have \"R04 修訂性質（bounded repair）\" and \"R06 修訂性質（bounded repair）\". Is that a contradiction? Not necessarily — R04 was indeed a bounded repair when written. Keeping it is factually accurate. But the reviewer finding #1 complained the file label lagged; the fix is to correctly label. Hmm.\n\nLet me think about what the future reviewer would want. Requirement 1 explicitly: \"update §0's revision summary so R06 is current and R05/R04 are historical\". It does NOT say update the R04 top note heading. So I'll follow literally: leave R04 heading as is. Actually wait — but then the R04 heading still reads \"（bounded repair）\", and a reviewer might say R04 should be historical. But the patch is explicit about what to change. Over-changing would violate \"Strict preservation\" (\"do not rewrite history\", \"beyond the exact revision/provenance notes requested above\").\n\nHmm, but \"the exact revision/provenance notes requested above\" — the requested notes are the R06 note and R05 note. So I should only ADD these two notes and modify title/§0/closing marker.\n\nDecision: Keep the existing R04/R03/R02 note headings and text unchanged. Add R06 and R05 notes above them.\n\nHmm, but wait: would leaving R04's heading as \"（bounded repair）\" conflict with R06's \"（bounded repair）\"? A careful reviewer might note two \"bounded repair\" labels. But the patch explicitly says preserve R04. Actually, let me reconsider: requirement says update §0 so \"R05/R04 are historical\". The top notes are part of revision provenance. Hmm.\n\nLet me look at how R05's own patch handled adding R05... actually R05 didn't add a note (that's the defect). Let me look at how R04's patch/receipt handled the R04 note. The R04 note was added by the R04 build. Let me check the R04 patch to see the exact convention for adding a new revision note while demoting the previous one.\n\nLet me read the R04 patch (0057_BLUEPRINT_REPAIR_PATCH_R04.md).\n\nActually, I realize the R05 file's top notes: the R04 note says \"本檔承接 R03 候選之內容，套用五項可逆 bounded repair\". So when R04 was created, they added the R04 note (bounded repair) and the R03 note became \"（歷史）\". Let me verify: In R05, the R03 note is labeled \"（歷史）\", and R02 note is labeled \"（歷史）\". So the pattern is: current revision = （bounded repair）, previous = （歷史）.\n\nSo by that established pattern, now that R06 is current, R05 is current-1, and R04 should become (歷史). Given the pattern, requirement \"R05/R04 are historical\" strongly implies the R04 top-note heading should also become （歷史）. And R05's new note is labeled （歷史） already per the patch.\n\nHmm, but requirement 1 says \"Preserve prior R04/R05 history and accurate labels such as `R04 欄名一致化`\". The \"accurate labels such as R04 欄名一致化\" are the inline §7 labels, not the top heading. So I think it's fine/expected to change the R04 top heading to `R04 修訂性質（歷史）`.\n\nHmm, this is a judgment call. Let me consider: the reviewer finding #1 says: \"rename labels to R05 and add one `R05 修訂性質` line naming only the T1 schema fix.\" So the pattern from the reviewer is: current revision label + 「RXX 修訂性質」line. The reviewer labeled it `R05 修訂性質` without specifying （bounded repair） or （歷史）. The patch says: add \"R05 修訂性質（歷史）\".\n\nI think the cleanest, most-likely-intended result:\n- Title: R06\n- Blockquote: R06 修訂性質（bounded repair） [new], R05 修訂性質（歷史） [new], R04 修訂性質（歷史） [relabeled heading], R03 修訂性質（歷史） [unchanged], R02 修訂性質（歷史） [unchanged]\n\nWait, but is relabeling R04 heading \"rewriting history\"? It's a label change. Hmm. The instruction \"do not rewrite history\" likely means don't alter the substance of past revision descriptions (the 5 points), don't claim R03/R04 did something different. Relabeling \"（bounded repair）\" → \"（歷史）\" is a version-status label, which is exactly what requirement 1 asks (\"R05/R04 are historical\").\n\nHmm, but requirement 1 says \"update §0's revision summary so R06 is current and R05/R04 are historical\" — only §0 mentioned. And \"add a concise current R06 修訂性質（bounded repair）note\". If I add R06 note labeled (bounded repair) and leave R04 labeled (bounded repair), the reader sees two